  "notes": [
    "The same attacker ran the Polygon leg 1,060 s before the Ethereum one, so Polygon anchors. A later Upgraded event re-set the same implementation without changing the route; the MONO pool's OFFICIAL status, needed for the MONO sales (zero insurance), predates the upgrade.",
    "Victims are the MonoXPool vaults on both chains plus the LPs whose liquidity the attacker force-removed (their MONO receipts net against the pool). DUCK has no DefiLlama token price and is valued at its CoinGecko price; the attacker still holds it. Ethereum MONO uses the Polygon MONO price."
